			"20": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "CONSTRUCTING TEXTURES\n\nThe Texture from Channels node can be used to construct a Texture2Drgba type out of Texture2Dchannels.\nThe Texture from Data node can be used to construct a Texture2Dchannel type out of data.\n\nWhen converting data into channels, at the default 8-bit(int) setting, all values equal and above 1 will be white and all values equal and below 0 will be black. This can be really useful when doing video synthesis as we can convert float-producing oscillators into visuals.\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 734.58111572265625,
					"width": 1049.185546875,
					"x": 1316.141357421875,
					"y": 55.08449172973632812
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Group",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"21": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TEXTURES\n\nIn the basic Texture tutorials you've learned about the Texture2Drgba type.\nYou know that Textures are made out of pixels and can be combined using the Video Mixer, Crossfader and Transition nodes.\n\nIn this tutorial we'll take a deep dive into the Texture2Dchannel type by deconstructing the Texture2Drgba type into separate channels. We will also show you how to use logic and mathematical operations on textures."
					}
				},
